<article class="env-definition" id="0E0V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E0V">Definition <span data-tag="0E0V">76.26.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume the fibres of $f$ are locally Noetherian (Divisors on Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/0CUX" data-tag="0CUX">71.4.2</a>). </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $x \in |X|$, and $y = f(x)$. We say that $f$ is <em>Cohen-Macaulay at $x$</em> if $f$ is flat at $x$ and the equivalent conditions of Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/04NC" data-tag="04NC">67.22.5</a> hold for the property $\mathcal{P}$ described in Lemma <a href="/tag/0E0U" data-tag="0E0U">76.26.1</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is a <em>Cohen-Macaulay morphism</em> if $f$ is Cohen-Macaulay at every point of $X$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>